stem of Penicillium echinulatum, which has been identified as a potential cellulase producer for bioconversion processes.\nL175: ### Preparation Note\nL176: \nL177: For TLC, simply blend a 15-20% aqueous slurry for about one minute and coat plates; dry at room temperature. Usually does not require activation before use.\nL178: \nL179: ### Legal Information\nL180: \nL181: * * *\nL182: \nL183: ## Compare Similar Items\nL184: \nL185: 【16†View Full Comparison】\nL186: \nL187: * * *\nL188: \nL189: Show Differences\nL190: \nL191: [Input]\nL192: \nL193: 1 of 1\nL194: ###### This Item\nL195:  | S6790  | S3504  | C6429\nL196: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL197: 【17†Sigma-Aldrich S5504 Sigmacell Cellulose】[Button: Quick View]  | 【18†Sigma-Aldrich S6790 Sigmacell Cellulose】[Button: Quick View]  | 【19†Sigma-Aldrich S3504 Sigmacell Cellulose】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich C6429 α-Cellulose】[Button: Quick View]\nL198: description Type 50, 50 μm  | description Type 101, Highly purified, fibers  | description Type 20, 20 μm  | description BioReagent, suitable for insect cell culture\nL199: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200\nL200: particle size 50 μm  | particle size-  | particle size 20 μm  | particle size-\nL201: type Type 50  | type Type 101  | type Type 20  | type-\nL202: * * *\nL203: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL204: \nL205: Explore all of our products under 【21†Sigmacell Cellulose】\nL206: \nL207: 【21†View All Products】\nL208: \nL209: * * *\nL210: \nL211: ## Safety Information\nL212: \nL213: ### Storage Class\nL214: \nL215: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL216: \nL217: ### WGK\nL218: \nL219: WGK 1\nL220: \nL221: ### Flash Point (°F)\nL222: \nL223: Not applicable\nL224: \nL225: ### Flash Point (°C)\nL226: \nL227: Not applicable\nL228: \nL229: ### PPE (personal protective equipment)\nL230: \nL231: Eyeshields, Gloves, type N95 (US)\nL232: \nL233: * * *\nL234: \nL235: ## Documentation\nL236: \nL237: [Button: Certificate of An